      "marks_pos": 2.0,
      "marks_neg": 0.5,
      "question": "What is the x-intercept of line joining (4, 2) and (6, 3)?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "text": "0"
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "text": "1"
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "text": "2"
        },
        {
          "label": "4",
          "text": "3"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "1",
      "solution": "Calculation:\n\nLet X₁ = 4, X₂ = 6, Y₁ = 2 & Y₂ = 3\n\nEquation of line\n\n⇒ (Y - Y₁) = (Y₂ - Y₁)/(X₂ - X₁₎) × (X - X₁)\n\n⇒ (Y - 2) = (3 - 2) /(6 - 4) × (X - 4)\n\n⇒ 2Y - 4 = X - 4\n\n⇒ X - 2Y = 0\n\n⇒ X = 2Y\n\nAt X intercept, Y = 0\n\n**∴ X = 0**",
      "tags": [
        "Geometry"
      ]
    },
